  "notes": "T53 is a rewrite of the module; this list is from my comments before and after. Expected also: many new kind entries (typedefs) as new entries telling nobody, which I have not listed one by one (ProviderLimitRefusal, FieldRefusal, ThresholdInvalidRefusal, NotAPayingAccountRefusal, UsageCost, Label, LabelServed, HealthTurn, MoneyByUnit, OwnLimitReached, ProviderLimitStanding, SwitchRequest, SwitchEstimate, SpanCost, MemberUse, UseByMember, ProviderLimitRequest, ProviderLimitRecorded, ProviderLimitShown, ProviderLimits, ThresholdRequest, ThresholdSet, ThresholdCrossed, Comparison, ReconcileRequest, Reconciled, RetestState, RetestRequest, RetestCapReached, RetestingOff, HealthShareState, HealthReport, AiUseNewWordKey, 12 row kinds, 4 answer unions). The tool lists AiUse's private #members as class members; if it compares them it will also report: removed AiUse##isSignin, AiUse##entryRefusal, AiUse.#callsOf, AiUse.#costOf (static), AiUse.#sums; new AiUse##entryOf, ##catalogue, ##carryDollars, ##countAct, ##usdUsed, ##usedFor, ##usdLimitBears, ##planMoney, ##ownerMoney, ##entry, ##entryMeasurable, ##unitUnavailable, ##amountOf, ##providerStanding, ##providerReached, ##moneyOf, ##figures, ##actsOwned, ##costOf, ##thresholdInvalid, ##noteCrossed, ##retestUsed, ##retestRow, ##retestOf, ##admin, ##healthReports, AiUse.#labelOf, .#usageOf, .#micro, .#where, .#who, .#priced, .#unstatedOf; changed ##exploreOf, ##estimate, ##used, ##accountsBar and others. By the method these tell nobody (no other module can reach them). AI_USE_TABLES and AI_USE_SCHEMA change only in content (new tables), so no kind change. Two bound changes are mine to make the comments true (LimitRequest's usd rule; LimitReachedRefusal's word for re-test caps). The real behaviour change most likely to break users: exploreAllowed/exploreAsk/useCheck(explore) now need account_id (without it explore reads no), and estimate's 'not known yet' string became an object; I expect the tool to see the second (hands back differently) but the first only as a bound change on a new parameter (the kind 'accepts more')."
 },
